# Copy to .env.production (or .env.local) and adjust as needed.
#
# Dev server (`npm run dev`) does NOT need this file — vite.config.js
# proxies /api/* to http://localhost:8000 automatically.
#
# A production build (`npm run build`) has no dev-server proxy, so the
# backend origin must be baked in explicitly, UNLESS the frontend is served
# from the same origin as the API (leave empty — relative /api/... works
# as-is). This is true for:
#   - The Desktop app (desktop_app/main.py serves this build's files and
#     the API from the same FastAPI process).
#   - A Web deployment behind a reverse proxy that also serves the backend
#     under the same origin.
# Set this only for a Web deployment where the frontend and backend are on
# different hosts — the backend's public URL.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=
